 _Avoid_: program (the websocket API's term), sketch, script.
 
 **FastLED Pattern** (local fork):
-A **Pattern** written in C++ against the FastLED library instead of the Pixelblaze language, marked by the first-line directive `// @pxlblz-language fastled` (optional `// @pxlblz-dim 1|2|3` and `// @pxlblz-output wire|leds`). The marker rides in `src`, so storage, autosave and navigation treat it like any Pattern. PXLBLZ-IDE compiles it through the **FastLED compile service** to wasm and previews real FastLED in the browser; with external pixel output on, its exact wire bytes go to the LED router (Art-Net/Fadecandy). It is never sent to a **Controller**, never part of a **Show**, never bundled into an artifact, and the agent does not discover it. Its FastLED `UISlider`/`UICheckbox`/`UINumberField` elements are its **Controls**, persisted per Pattern by UI name.
+A **Pattern** written in C++ against the FastLED library instead of the Pixelblaze language, marked by the first-line directive `// @pxlblz-language fastled` (optional `// @pxlblz-dim 1|2|3` and `// @pxlblz-output wire|leds`). The marker rides in `src`, so storage, autosave and navigation treat it like any Pattern. PXLBLZ-IDE compiles it through the **FastLED compile service** to wasm and previews real FastLED in the browser; with external pixel output on, its exact wire bytes go to the LED router (Art-Net/Fadecandy). It is never sent to a **Controller**, never part of a **Show**, never bundled into an artifact, and the agent does not discover it. Its FastLED `UISlider`/`UICheckbox`/`UINumberField` elements are its **Controls**, persisted per Pattern by UI name. It may hold supporting files (`.h`, `.cpp`, further `.ino`), kept in the same `src` as `// @pxlblz-file <path>` sections and edited as file tabs.
 _Avoid_: sketch (FastLED's own word) in UI and docs; calling the LED router a Controller.
 
+**FastLED example** (local fork):
+One of the official FastLED examples in the read-only built-in "FastLED" folder of the Patterns rail (vendored catalogue, built-in key `fastled:<id>`). It opens read-only like a stock demo and **Clone** turns it into a personal **FastLED Pattern**. Examples marked hardware (ESP32 drivers, audio input, …) stay listed with their note and may not compile or show anything on the PC.
+_Avoid_: demo sketch; calling it a stock Pattern (stock Patterns are Pixelblaze).
+
 **FastLED compile service**:
 The local helper (`fastled-integration/service/server.mjs`, default `http://127.0.0.1:9996`) that turns FastLED Pattern source plus defines (`PXLBLZ_NUM_LEDS` = the map's pixel count) into a wasm module and compiler diagnostics. Started by the Art-Net launcher; when it is not reachable the preview says so and the editor keeps saving.
 
